--- a/src/apu/README.md
+++ b/src/apu/README.md
@@ -3,21 +3,40 @@
 Hardware emulation of the Xbox's MCPX APU (Audio Processing Unit), extracted from [xemu](https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu). The APU is a custom chip with three processors:
 
 - **VP (Voice Processor)** — 256 hardware voices, ADPCM/PCM decode, pitch shifting, envelopes, HRTF 3D audio
-- **GP (Global Processor)** — DSP for global effects (reverb, chorus). Currently **stubbed** — effects bypass.
-- **EP (Encode Processor)** — DSP for AC3/DTS encoding. Currently **stubbed** — passthrough.
+- **GP (Global Processor)** — DSP for global effects (reverb, chorus). Guest-visible X/Y/P RAM windows are mapped; DSP firmware execution remains incomplete.
+- **EP (Encode Processor)** — DSP for AC3/DTS encoding. Guest-visible X/Y/P RAM windows are mapped; DSP firmware execution remains incomplete.
 
 Audio output uses Windows `waveOut` at 48kHz stereo 16-bit.
 
+## DSP56300 FFI bridge status
+
+The optional `XBOXRECOMP_ENABLE_DSP56300` CMake setting builds the MIT-licensed
+`dsp56300-emu-ffi` static library from a separately checked-out upstream
+revision and creates GP/EP engine instances over the APU's existing backing
+arrays. The reviewed source revision is
+`82fb25a6917a36ac66212ae31f02aab62211f979`; set `DSP56300_SOURCE_DIR` to that
+clean checkout and make the Rust 1.99 toolchain available to CMake.
+
+The GP and EP RAM windows are routed through the APU MMIO handler, including
+the GP mixbuffer alias and 24-bit word masking. P-memory writes use the FFI
+write API when that engine is enabled so translated code is invalidated. The
+reset register is stored and reset assertion resets the core; reset release
+does not yet load firmware. Scratch bootstrap, cycle scheduling, peripheral
+callbacks, FIFO/DMA, and DSP audio remain unimplemented. The optional FFI core
+stays off by default, and this is not playable-audio support.
+
 ## Files
 
 | File | LOC | Purpose |
 |------|-----|---------|
 | `apu.h` | 70 | **Public API** — init, shutdown, MMIO, mixer voices |
-| `apu_state.h` | 525 | APU state struct (VP, GP, EP, DSP core, 256 voices) |
+| `apu_state.h` | 537 | APU state struct (VP, GP, EP, DSP core, 256 voices) |
 | `apu_regs.h` | 366 | MCPX APU register definitions and field masks |
 | `apu_core.c` | 762 | MMIO handlers, frame thread, waveOut output, test tone |
 | `apu_vp.c` | 1,247 | Voice Processor — decode, resample, mix, envelopes, HRTF |
-| `apu_dsp.c` | 90 | GP/EP stubs (mixbin 0/1 passthrough) |
+| `apu_dsp.c` | 259 | GP/EP lifecycle and current passthrough stub |
+| `apu_dsp56300_bridge.c` | 210 | GP/EP RAM map and optional FFI engine lifecycle |
+| `apu_dsp56300_bridge.h` | 17 | Bridge declarations |
 | `apu_mmio_hook.c` | 253 | VEH x86-64 instruction decoder for 0xFE800000+ MMIO |
 | `apu_shim.h` | 431 | QEMU compatibility (threads, atomics, clocks → Win32) |
 | `apu_debug.h` | 104 | Debug logging macros |
